{"/api/discogs/artist/137127/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"137127","image":"https://i.discogs.com/UklPl8GSKQsBN9nyCwYnKdSurcZkgNsiVcKsK3ZnqK4/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:414/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEzNzEy/Ny0xNzE1NzEzOTY1/LTE4NTcucG5n.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/Jx-oY9ygM7qBe54U6HnTdm4jn8SKCAH-iMgOvZMAa_w/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEzNzEy/Ny0xNzE1NzEzOTY1/LTE4NTcucG5n.jpeg","profile":"Suicidal Tendencies is a US-based hardcore punk and metal band. The band was formed in 1981 in Venice, California by vocalist Mike Muir. Since the band's inception, Muir has been the group's only constant member, although rhythm guitarist Mike Clark was with the group from 1988 until 2013. The group started off as hardcore punk act and their 1983 self-titled debut scored an unexpected hit with the song \"Institutionalized\", which went into heavy rotation on the poplar SoCal radio station KROQ. It was a full two years later in 1985 when a video was produced and got heavy airplay on MTV. Meanwhile, in 1984 the group was banned from performing live in the city of Los Angeles, citing concerns about crowd violence. The ban remained in effect until the early 1990s. By the end of the 1980s, the band had evolved into a full-fledged thrash metal band and would soon begin adding more funk influences into their music. In 1995, the group announced their split, marking the end to their most commercially successful period. Mike Muir and Mike Clark would resurrect the band in 1996 with new members and the group continues to this day, although their recorded output has been sparse since reuniting. \r\n\r\nThroughout Suicidal's career, Muir has fronted a number of side-projects like [a=Los Cycos], [a=No Mercy (3)], [a=Infectious Grooves], and his own solo act, [a=Cyco Miko]. These acts have usually featured other members of Suicidal, as well.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:137127","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":1985154,"name":"Cyco Nation"}],"groups":null,"members":[{"active":false,"id":251591,"name":"Dave Lombardo"},{"active":true,"id":267832,"name":"Mike Muir"},{"active":true,"id":268635,"name":"Benjamin Weinman"},{"active":false,"id":410710,"name":"Jimmy DeGrasso"},{"active":true,"id":419724,"name":"Dean Pleasants"},{"active":false,"id":436745,"name":"Amery Smith"},{"active":false,"id":470403,"name":"Grant Estes"},{"active":false,"id":470404,"name":"Louiche Mayorga"},{"active":false,"id":470406,"name":"R.J. Herrera"},{"active":false,"id":470407,"name":"Rocky George"},{"active":false,"id":470682,"name":"Mike Clark (5)"},{"active":false,"id":470683,"name":"Bob Heathcote"},{"active":false,"id":490079,"name":"Robert Trujillo"},{"active":false,"id":503867,"name":"Brooks Wackerman"},{"active":false,"id":504485,"name":"Josh Paul"},{"active":false,"id":522429,"name":"Ric Clayton"},{"active":false,"id":774300,"name":"Ronald Bruner Jr."},{"active":false,"id":1031636,"name":"Thomas Pridgen"},{"active":false,"id":1425541,"name":"Michael Dunnigan"},{"active":false,"id":1425542,"name":"Sean Dunnigan"},{"active":false,"id":1513503,"name":"Jon Nelson (2)"},{"active":false,"id":1516335,"name":"Eric Moore (3)"},{"active":false,"id":1573878,"name":"Stephen Bruner"},{"active":false,"id":1674458,"name":"Jay Weinberg"},{"active":false,"id":2090699,"name":"David Hidalgo Jr."},{"active":false,"id":2954164,"name":"Rick Battson"},{"active":false,"id":3217177,"name":"Nico Santora"},{"active":false,"id":3217179,"name":"Tim Williams (22)"},{"active":true,"id":3572041,"name":"Ra Diaz"},{"active":false,"id":5291306,"name":"Jeff Pogan"},{"active":false,"id":6029273,"name":"Brandon Pertzborn"},{"active":false,"id":11344628,"name":"Greyson Nekrutman"},{"active":true,"id":12866645,"name":"Tye Trujillo"}],"namevariations":["S.T.","ST","Suicidal","Suisidal Tendences"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/137127-Suicidal-Tendencies","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.suicidaltendencies.com","https://www.facebook.com/suicidaltendencies","https://www.instagram.com/suicidaltendencies","https://www.youtube.com/@suicidaltendencies/videos","http://www.myspace.com/suicidaltendencies","http://twitter.com/OFFICIALSTIG","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suicidal_Tendencies"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/14185/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"14185","image":"https://i.discogs.com/3tB9-H0swNFclPxygiKHkjOhVpr8-dNnGX8fFqS1CX4/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:425/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE0MTg1/LTE2MTcxMzc4OTgt/MjU1My5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/Yeacr0AQEH5D5hMyaTE7LSycS86AN6Iom713qy2Ir4k/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE0MTg1/LTE2MTcxMzc4OTgt/MjU1My5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"American boogie-soul funk group, formed in a Brooklyn, New York City high school in the early 1980s by [a=James \"D-Train\" Williams] (lead vocals) and [a=Hubert Eaves III] (keyboards, bass, drums and arrangements). They garnered much success on the early 1980s disco scene. \r\nFusing gospel-influenced vocals with tight synth-funk production, they quickly became trailblazers of the post-disco era. Their sound was defined by pulsating basslines, shimmering keys, and uplifting hooks, as heard on timeless club anthems like \"You're the One for Me\", \"Keep On\", and \"Something's on Your Mind\".","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:14185","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":34858,"name":"Hubert Eaves III"},{"active":true,"id":67214,"name":"James \"D-Train\" Williams"}],"namevariations":["\"D\" TRAIN","\"D\" Train","\"D\" Train Band, The","\"D\"Train","\"D-Train\"","''D'' Train","'D' Train","'D'-Train","D Train","D' Train","D'Train","D. Train","D.Train","D:Train","DTrain","Disco Train","Dr. Train","Dtrain","J.D.Train","The \"D\" Train Band","Train","«D» Train","“D” Train"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/14185-D-Train","type":"artist","urls