"Jamie McKenna"}],"groups":[{"active":true,"id":15662121,"name":"The Accidental Choir"}],"members":null,"namevariations":["J. Woon","WOON","Woon"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/747927-Jamie-Woon","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.jamiewoon.com","https://www.facebook.com/jamiewoonmusic","https://twitter.com/jamiewoon","https://www.instagram.com/jamiewoon","https://myspace.com/jamiewoon","http://www.songkick.com/artists/205014-jamie-woon","https://open.spotify.com/artist/1fUMEn4Yk7ZUloozE0fRLL","https://soundcloud.com/woon","https://www.youtube.com/user/jamiewoon","https://www.youtube.com/user/JamieWoonVEVO","http://www.dailymotion.com/JamieWoon-vevo","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamie_Woon","https://music.apple.com/us/artist/jamie-woon/166541433"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/95966/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"95966","image":"https://i.discogs.com/dth5hTuvgU3G77Vy7bWEg3D5kFcVRmpKHLAFAnBnNsA/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:393/w:579/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTk1OTY2/LTE0NzE1MDYyMjkt/ODkyOC5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/xnKjut5W8-cLlTfGx7EzFnb43EXuJ9uFDvtUpackk3M/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTk1OTY2/LTE0NzE1MDYyMjkt/ODkyOC5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"Jamaican reggae vocal group, first comprised of Winston 'Pipe' Matthews on lead vocals, Lloyd 'Bread' McDonald, and George 'Buddy' Haye, the Wailing Souls carried the moniker of the Renegades during the late 1960’s. This line-up recorded backing vocals for an Ernest Ranglin album before breaking up in 1968.\r\n'Pipe' and 'Bread' teamed up with two other singers after that, Oswald Downer and Norman Davis, and they went on to work with Coxsone Dodd's famous Studio One label recording label. They recorded a number of singles there, and were also billed as the Classics, in addition to their Wailing Souls name.\r\nIn the early 70's, the Souls recorded for Bob Marley's Tuff Gong label, as Pipe and The Pipers.  The group’s vocal power, and song writing ability has kept the group in the spotlight, and in 1974 the group changed again when Downes and Davis left and 'Buddy' Haye rejoined.\r\nThe group entered another era of their careers as they began work with famed producer \"Jo Jo\" Hookim and his Channel One label. The Souls then started their own label in 1977, Massive. In the early 80's the now quartet (with the addition of Rudolph ‘Garth’ Dennis from Black Uhuru fame) worked with a number of hot producers including Sly and Robbie, \"Junjo\" Lawes' and Linval Thompson.\r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:95966","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":3150167,"name":"Pipe & The Pipers"},{"id":3324272,"name":"Matsimela"},{"id":3669389,"name":"The Classics (12)"},{"id":4003108,"name":"Attamas"}],"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":394644,"name":"Winston \"Pipe\" Matthews"},{"active":true,"id":394645,"name":"Lloyd \"Bread\" McDonald"},{"active":true,"id":443703,"name":"George \"Buddy\" Haye"},{"active":false,"id":443704,"name":"Rudolph \"Garth\" Dennis"},{"active":true,"id":2945099,"name":"T. Anderson (3)"},{"active":false,"id":3162757,"name":"Norman Anthony Davis"},{"active":false,"id":4249180,"name":"Devon Beckford"},{"active":false,"id":7940347,"name":"Oswald Downer"}],"namevariations":["Soul Dimensions","The Wailing Soul","The Wailing Souls","The Wailing Souls)","The Walling Souls","W. Soul","W. Souls","Wail Souls","Wailin Souls","Wailin\" Souls","Wailing Soul","Wailing Souls, The","Wailing Sound","Waiting Soul","Waling Souls","Willing.S"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/95966-Wailing-Souls","type":"artist","urls":["https://thewailingsouls.bandcamp.com/","https://wailingsouls.bandcamp.com/","https://www.imdb.com/name/nm3056707/","https://www.facebook.com/wailingsoulsmusic","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Wailing_Souls"]}},"/api/discogs/label/1071/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"1071","image":"https://i.discogs.com/8x55anzBTLcofS2gd_c7c1SgL-hgoC4f7JBbkQ74tUs/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:277/w:240/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTEwNzEt/MTQwNTU5Mjg4MC0y/MDE4LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/ePtHWA_pMcnWypB0M0Lfhsb_ie7SNASjv_v-pC01vm8/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTEwNzEt/MTQwNTU5Mjg4MC0y/MDE4LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"US label launched by [a=Dave Grusin] and [a=Larry Rosen] as the successor to [l=Arista GRP] when their partnership with [l362] ended circa November 1982.\r\nLabel Code: [b]LC 6713 / LC 06713[/b].\r\nThe label's acts included [a=Dave Valentin] and jazz-funk trumpeter [a=Tom Browne].\r\n\r\nIn February 1990, the label's parent company, [l=GRP Records Inc.] was sold to MCA and GRP became an MCA label although it had been distributed in the US by MCA from March 1987 onwards.\r\nGRP became known early on for digital recordings and for being one of the first US labels to release its albums on CD, becoming known as [l3804794].\r\n\r\nGRP initially meant [i][b]G[/b]rusin-[b]R[/b]osen [b]P[/b]roductions[/i]. After Grusin and Rosen left the company in 1995, the letters became shorthand for the marketing slogan [b]G[/b][i]reat[/i] [b]R[/b][i]ecords[/i] [b]P[/b][i]eriod[/i].\r\n\r\nGRP is currently part of the [l=The Verve Music Group] and is mostly used for reissues.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:1071","relations":{"parentLabel":{"id":195155,"name":"The Verve Music Group"},"sublabels":[{"id":3285315,"name":"A Chess Reissue"},{"id":369808,"name":"Chessmates"},{"id":566676,"name":"Gold Encore Series"},{"id":691349,"name":"GRP 10th Anniversary"},{"id":482552,"name":"GRP Christmas Collection"},{"id":369768,"name":"GRP Presents The Legendary Masters Of Jazz"},{"id":577965,"name":"Priceless Jazz Collection"},{"id":1864681,"name":"Sounds Of (2)"},{"id":586213,"name":"The Original American Decca Recordings"},{"id":1485525,"name":"The Very Best Of GRP"}]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/1071-GRP","type":"label","urls":["https://www.facebook.com/grprecords/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GRP_Records","http://www.absoluteastronomy.com/topics/GRP_Records#encyclopedia"]}},"/api/discogs/label/3981681/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"3981681","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:3981681","relations":{"parentLabel":null,"sublabels":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/3981681-781-Records","type":"label","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/label/76974/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"76974","image":"https://i.discogs.com/FvtTp7XqqJL1qdoZtE_iDpADYUe8Ov4jfDd4bM6Xudw/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:202/w:191/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTc2OTc0/LTEyODU4OTkzODQu/anBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/vHQpYuasWHvP-iSZxmTSEVqazu-FwRkrutgQdSXeO-E/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTc2OTc0/LTEyODU4OTkzODQu/anBlZw.jpeg","profile":"\r\nCanadian trade name of the Canadian division of EMI Music Group (See note below).\r\nPlease also add any branded labels if they appear on the release.\r\nIf credited that way on unofficial releases, please use [l925499] instead.\r\n\r\nEMI Music Canada ceased its operations after it was acquired by the [l38404] in September 2012. Its successor is [l173994].\r\n\r\nIt included a manufacturing facility inherited from [l185318] and which was renamed to [l76974] in 1993.\r\n\r\nThe vinyl pressing and tape duplication plant was opened next door to the offices in June 1976. It had 17 presses for albums and seven presses for singles. The plant started production with singles only in June and began pressing albums in October 1976.  The plant stopped pressing vinyl on July 13, 1984 but did continue its tape duplication operations.\r\n\r\nThe CD pressing plant was built between Dec. 1994 and Aug. 1995. It closed Feb 20, 2007.\r\n\r\nGlass mastering was not done at the plant – The negative imprinted “stampers” were delivered to the plant so that replication could be undertaken by them.\r\n\r\nEMI Music Canada ultimately had two dual line CD replication units, enabling one line to manufacture two different selections at a time.  A total of 11.3 million units were being manufactured annually by Fiscal '98.\r\n\r\n[b]History:[/b]\r\n\r\n1947 - 1954 [l=Capitol Records Of Canada, Ltd.]\r\n1954 - 1958 [l=Capitol Records Distributors Of Canada, Ltd.]\r\n1958 - 1966 [l=Capitol Records Of Canada, Ltd.]\r\n1966 - 1974 [l=Capitol Records (Canada) Ltd.]\r\n1974 - 1993 [l=Capitol Records-EMI Of Canada Limited] a.k.a. [l=Capitol Records-EMI Of Canada]\r\n1993 - 2012 Sept. [l=EMI Music Canada]\r\n\r\n[b]Plant Indicators for CD's[/b]\r\n\r\nThe plant can be identified by a combination of the following indicators.\r\n•\t\"MANUFACTURED BY EMI MUSIC CANADA\" in the matrix (example [r3063100]).\r\n•\tCommonly credited on release artwork as \"MANUFACTURED BY EMI MUSIC CANADA\" (example [r2341468]).\r\n•\tA sequential ‘E’ number (use commencing in the 2nd half of 2004) with the following formats E#####-# / E#####L / E### ##-# (examples [r25998358], [r699877], [r14768153]).\r\n         Nb. The appended #/L appears to indicate the glass master.\r\n•\tUse of this plants press SID code IFPI 1F** (use of this code ceased with the plants closure in 2007)\r\n•\tUsed glass masters produced by the following plants.\r\n\r\n[l271397]\r\nMastering SID Codes (Up to approximately 1998)\r\nIFPI L481 to IFPI L483.\r\n\r\n[l294033]\r\nMastering SID Codes (Up to plants closure in 2004)\r\nIFPI L043, IFPI L044.\r\n\r\n[l635272]\r\nMastering SID Codes (Between 2004 to 2006)\r\nIFPI L383, L384, L385, L388\r\n\r\n[l4081986]\r\nMastering SID Code (Up to plants closure in 2011)\r\nIFPI LW60\r\n\r\n\r\n[b]LCCN Roles[/b]\r\n\r\nPressed By if IFPI 1F** used.\r\nOtherwise, if “MANUFACTURED BY EMI MUSIC CANADA ” is in the matrix use the Manufactured By role.\r\n\r\nThe sequential 'E' number 'E##### (do not enter the appended '-# or 'L') can also be entered as the cat# for these roles.\r\n\r\nWhere glass masters produced by [l271397], [l294033], [l635272] or [l4081986] are used an additional Glass Mastered At role may also be applicable. Please check these profiles for guidance in this regard.\r\n\r\n\r\n[b]Note:[/b]\r\n\r\nMarch 1988 the official Canadian company name was registered as TEMI Canada Inc. (TEMI standing for [l118508].)\r\nJan. 1997 TEMI Canada Inc. was changed to to EMI Group Canada Inc.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:76974","relations":{"parentLabel":{"id":45746,"name":"EMI Music"},"sublabels":[{"id":1129104,"name":"Anne Murray Signature Series"},{"id":879172,"name":"EMI Music Canada Special Markets"},{"id":831992,"name":"Man Of the Land Collection"},{"id":74361,"name":"Maximum Music Group"},{"id":580759,"name":"Valu Plus"}]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/76974-EMI-Music-Canada","type":"label","urls":["https://web.archive.org/web/19990128113225/http://emimusic.ca:80/index_main.html","http://www.emigroup.com"]}},"/api/discogs/release/1036821":{"cached":true,"release":{"artists":[{"id":null,"name":"Afroman"}],"formats":[],"genres":["Hip Hop"],"id":"1036821","images":[],"labels":[{"catno":"LOAF 20102","id":4318,"name":"T-Bones Records"}],"styles":["Pop Rap"],"title":"Sell Your Dope","tracklist":["Basehead Boogie","Palmdale","Crazy Rap","Let's All Get Drunk","If It Ain't Free","Sell Your Dope","There's A Price 2 Pay","Paranoid","Strugglin' N' Strivin'","Let Me Out","Bacc 2 School","Hungry Hustler","God Has Smiled On Me"],"uri":"https://www.discogs.com/release/1036821","videos":[],"year":2000}},"/api/discogs/release/10507310/credits":{"cached":true,"credits":[{"id":3147696,"name":"Nick Wisdom","role":"Main Artist","type":"artist"},{"id":7680,"name":"Bastard Jazz Recordings","role":"Label","type":"label"},{"id":3605205,"name":"Nate Drobner","role":"Producer","type":"person"},{"id":3147696,"name":"Nick Wisdom","role":"Producer","type":"person